<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duleep Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Maharaja Duleep Singh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duleep Singh was the last maharaja of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, installed as a child after the violent succession struggles that followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>'s death. After the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> wars the British annexed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in 1849, and he was removed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, where he spent most of his life in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duleep-singh.jpg" alt="Duleep Singh" width="275" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Capt. Goldingham of London. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharajah_Duleep_Singh_dressed_for_a_State_function,_c._1875.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
